WEBVTT

00:00:12.620 --> 00:00:14.200
"Three Days Have Passed Since Jack's Murder"

00:00:14.200 --> 00:00:15.160
"Revenge For His Sister?
The People of the Moran Murder Incident"

00:00:15.160 --> 00:00:16.700
"Tragic Hero?
Ward Mayor Moran's Son James"

00:00:16.910 --> 00:00:21.200
My son... James...
has done something unforgivable.

00:00:21.200 --> 00:00:26.160
But... he just wanted to avenge his sister!

00:00:27.620 --> 00:00:29.910
"Jack's True Identity Was..."

00:00:29.950 --> 00:00:31.120
"Disguised Himself as Hokari Maki (A woman)"

00:00:33.330 --> 00:00:38.500
A teenager killed Jack the Ripper? Holy shit.

00:00:38.500 --> 00:00:41.250
James is super hot!

00:00:41.250 --> 00:00:45.580
Suspect James Moran killed
the man who killed his sister...

00:00:53.910 --> 00:00:59.250
James avenged Alex, huh?

00:00:59.250 --> 00:01:00.910
Irene- <i>san</i> ...

00:01:00.910 --> 00:01:05.330
Did you know Moriarty from before?

00:01:05.330 --> 00:01:07.500
Yes.

00:01:07.500 --> 00:01:10.080
I was Alex's tutor.

00:01:10.080 --> 00:01:11.410
I brought you some tea!

00:01:11.410 --> 00:01:13.660
Thanks, James!

00:01:15.040 --> 00:01:20.040
She was sick and frail.
Almost never left her room.

00:01:20.040 --> 00:01:26.080
And the one day she did leave
the house, Jack killed her...

00:01:26.080 --> 00:01:29.500
It always seemed weird to me.

00:01:29.500 --> 00:01:34.790
That's why I thought Moran
might be involved with Jack.

00:01:36.120 --> 00:01:38.910
So you stole the USB drive.

00:01:38.910 --> 00:01:40.700
Yes.

00:01:40.700 --> 00:01:46.040
You were right. Moran was
hiring Jack to do his dirty work.

00:01:46.040 --> 00:01:48.950
The USB had the data proving it.

00:01:48.950 --> 00:01:55.080
But Jack destroyed it, and now any way
of proving Moran's guilt is gone.

00:01:56.540 --> 00:02:00.540
Alex got caught between the two of them, huh?

00:02:00.540 --> 00:02:03.120
Yeah, probably.

00:02:08.580 --> 00:02:11.330
Okay, I'm heading back inside.

00:02:14.750 --> 00:02:15.910
Thanks.

00:02:15.910 --> 00:02:19.040
This cleared up a lot of things.

00:02:20.120 --> 00:02:22.620
It's me. Good to talk to you again.

00:02:22.620 --> 00:02:25.750
Yes. Yes.

00:02:27.830 --> 00:02:33.160
Why don't you tell Irene- <i>san</i> and the rest
of the row house what really happened?

00:02:33.160 --> 00:02:38.160
Moriarty wanted to hide the truth.

00:02:38.160 --> 00:02:41.540
Please, Sherlock Holmes.

00:02:50.040 --> 00:02:56.120
Ward Mayor Moran really wanted to kill Moriarty.

00:02:56.120 --> 00:02:59.540
I can't believe a man
would want to kill his own son...

00:02:59.540 --> 00:03:02.410
We'll never know the truth.

00:03:02.410 --> 00:03:06.830
I'm sure that Moriarty didn't want to know.

00:03:06.830 --> 00:03:09.950
Hey, old man. What's with the gloomy look?

00:03:09.950 --> 00:03:15.540
It just doesn't make sense.
How Moriarty killed Jack, I mean...

00:03:15.540 --> 00:03:19.500
Well, he had a knife to the throat
of the man who killed his sister.

00:03:19.500 --> 00:03:23.040
He wasn't thinking straight.

00:03:23.040 --> 00:03:23.950
Maybe...

00:03:23.950 --> 00:03:29.200
So you're worried about Moriarty, huh?

00:03:29.200 --> 00:03:31.410
Worried? No, I'm not...

00:03:31.410 --> 00:03:33.870
It's fine. I understand.

00:03:33.870 --> 00:03:36.870
You've known him a lot longer than me.

00:03:36.870 --> 00:03:39.160
I'm not worried, okay?

00:03:39.160 --> 00:03:41.410
Your best friend just vanished...

00:03:41.410 --> 00:03:44.330
I can't even imagine how you must feel.

00:03:44.330 --> 00:03:48.790
No, list--

00:03:44.330 --> 00:03:48.790
I still can't believe Moriarty would...

00:03:50.330 --> 00:03:54.000
You're still not going back to the West Side?

00:03:54.000 --> 00:03:57.500
Jack is dead. The USB drive is gone.

00:03:57.500 --> 00:04:01.450
There's no reason for Moran to go after you now.

00:04:01.450 --> 00:04:05.580
Well, maybe you're right, but...

00:04:09.660 --> 00:04:11.410
There's a new job.

00:04:11.410 --> 00:04:13.950
Pipe...

00:04:13.950 --> 00:04:16.120
Pipe is...

00:04:16.120 --> 00:04:19.080
I can't believe it!

00:05:50.620 --> 00:05:56.040
Pipe... Pipe is...

00:05:56.040 --> 00:05:59.700
"No More Nyan-Nyan"

00:05:56.040 --> 00:05:59.700
...missing since yesterday!

00:05:59.700 --> 00:06:04.330
He's never done this in his whole life!

00:06:04.330 --> 00:06:08.000
Maybe this guy cat-napped him!

00:06:08.000 --> 00:06:10.870
He's been going around Kabukicho

00:06:10.870 --> 00:06:15.290
kidnapping people's pets and
selling them for a lot of money!

00:06:17.250 --> 00:06:21.790
Would he go for a cat that big?

00:06:21.790 --> 00:06:25.330
To be honest, I feel like
I've got bigger problems.

00:06:25.330 --> 00:06:27.830
Moririn is...

00:06:27.830 --> 00:06:32.410
I can't forgive Maki... I mean, Jack!

00:06:32.410 --> 00:06:35.120
He got what he deserved when he died!

00:06:40.700 --> 00:06:43.580
I'm hiring you to find Pipe!

00:06:43.580 --> 00:06:47.750
Everybody in this room is taking the job,
whether you like it or not!

00:06:47.750 --> 00:06:50.620
We have to do it?

00:06:50.620 --> 00:06:53.580
When the sun sets in other towns,

00:06:53.580 --> 00:06:56.790
in our town the neon lights turn on.

00:06:56.790 --> 00:06:59.290
You may want gold and silver,

00:06:59.290 --> 00:07:02.330
but find my goddamn cat!

00:07:02.330 --> 00:07:04.580
A light shines in the detectives' eyes.

00:07:04.580 --> 00:07:07.410
This row house is filled with
the strangest of men,

00:07:07.410 --> 00:07:12.000
and people call it "The Detective's Row House."

00:07:12.000 --> 00:07:13.950
This is a special A5 rank job!

00:07:13.950 --> 00:07:15.790
"A5 Top Grade Meat"

00:07:13.950 --> 00:07:15.790
This is a special A5 rank job!

00:07:15.790 --> 00:07:20.330
Top grade meat awaits the one
who brings back my Pipe!

00:07:20.330 --> 00:07:23.160
Ready... go!

00:07:24.160 --> 00:07:26.500
This is bullshit.

00:07:33.790 --> 00:07:35.080
Thanks.

00:07:35.080 --> 00:07:40.250
I hope they cheer up a bit...

00:07:49.910 --> 00:07:54.330
This can't be true... Maki- <i>chan</i> is Jack?

00:07:54.330 --> 00:07:56.080
It can't be...

00:07:58.290 --> 00:08:02.750
Tell me it's not true, Maki- <i>chan</i> ...

00:08:02.750 --> 00:08:04.580
Maki- <i>chan</i> !

00:08:06.580 --> 00:08:12.790
You're not going to look for Pipe?

00:08:12.790 --> 00:08:16.410
I can't believe Moririn lost his sister...

00:08:16.410 --> 00:08:20.700
I didn't even notice at all!

00:08:20.700 --> 00:08:23.790
How has he felt this whole time?

00:08:25.700 --> 00:08:29.830
She's the only sister I have.

00:08:29.830 --> 00:08:34.870
You have a sister too, right?
So you know how I feel.

00:08:34.870 --> 00:08:36.160
Yeah, I guess.

00:08:37.580 --> 00:08:41.200
When he gets back, I'm gonna
have something to say to him.

00:08:41.200 --> 00:08:47.080
"You idiot, why didn't you talk to us?"

00:08:47.080 --> 00:08:52.500
You can still help him when he comes back.

00:08:52.500 --> 00:08:58.040
For now, we've gotta do our job.
Let's look for Pipe.

00:09:04.580 --> 00:09:08.580
I'm not wasting my time on a job
that doesn't pay a single yen.

00:09:08.580 --> 00:09:12.290
Right? You think so too, right?

00:09:12.290 --> 00:09:14.370
Another win.

00:09:14.370 --> 00:09:15.620
Hey, Michel.

00:09:15.620 --> 00:09:17.200
Seems like you're making money today.

00:09:17.200 --> 00:09:18.370
I guess, yes.

00:09:18.370 --> 00:09:23.950
So, is it true that Jack the Ripper
was a regular at Pipe Cat?

00:09:23.950 --> 00:09:28.870
Moran's son, the guy who killed him,
went there a lot too, right?

00:09:28.870 --> 00:09:30.040
Yeah.

00:09:30.040 --> 00:09:33.040
The Ward Mayor's got it tough,
with a son like that.

00:09:33.040 --> 00:09:36.660
The news is saying he was
trying to avenge his sister.

00:09:36.660 --> 00:09:39.870
But he's still a murderer.

00:09:39.870 --> 00:09:42.000
What?

00:09:42.000 --> 00:09:44.790
I ain't a fan of Moran.

00:09:44.790 --> 00:09:49.330
But I know what it feels like when
somebody kills your daughter.

00:09:49.330 --> 00:09:52.330
And his son took vengeance for him.

00:09:52.330 --> 00:09:55.540
How is that not being a good son?

00:10:00.290 --> 00:10:02.660
It's raining money!

00:10:02.660 --> 00:10:04.500
Stop! Hey!

00:10:05.540 --> 00:10:07.160
That stupid cat!

00:10:07.160 --> 00:10:09.580
I'll turn it into a shamisen.

00:10:09.580 --> 00:10:11.330
What's this baby carriage?

00:10:11.330 --> 00:10:12.540
It looks so dumb.

00:10:12.540 --> 00:10:16.290
This is the only one Pipe could fit in.

00:10:16.290 --> 00:10:19.290
I'm not doing this because I want to.

00:10:19.290 --> 00:10:21.750
When's the captain coming back?

00:10:21.750 --> 00:10:25.200
I'm bored.

00:10:25.200 --> 00:10:26.700
Hey, you kids!

00:10:26.700 --> 00:10:28.540
Stop your whining and get to work!

00:10:28.540 --> 00:10:34.000
It's up to the Irregulars to protect
Kabukicho while Morairty's gone!

00:10:34.000 --> 00:10:41.410
Until Moriarty gets back, Yoshio,
I appoint you acting captain!

00:10:42.910 --> 00:10:45.750
Acting captain?

00:10:47.500 --> 00:10:51.660
Kobayashi. Mrs. Hudson's got
you looking for Pipe, right?

00:10:51.660 --> 00:10:52.790
Right.

00:10:52.790 --> 00:10:58.200
Mrs. Hudson's pretty down after what
happened with Moriarty and Maki.

00:10:58.200 --> 00:11:01.370
The least we can do is find that cat.

00:11:03.910 --> 00:11:06.870
Okay, this is my first order as acting captain!

00:11:06.870 --> 00:11:09.790
Let's find Pipe before Kobayashi does!

00:11:09.790 --> 00:11:11.250
Yes! Yeah!

00:11:11.250 --> 00:11:14.160
You're not helping me?

00:11:19.500 --> 00:11:21.450
"Thomas Shomaru Retirement Performance"

00:11:21.790 --> 00:11:26.370
Sherlock, you're not going
to go looking for Pipe?

00:11:26.370 --> 00:11:31.250
It's time for Thomas Shomaru's last
performance before his retirement!

00:11:31.250 --> 00:11:33.500
"Sold Out"

00:11:31.250 --> 00:11:33.500
I got the last ticket before it sold out!

00:11:33.500 --> 00:11:34.830
"Sold Out"

00:11:33.500 --> 00:11:34.830
Come on!

00:11:34.830 --> 00:11:38.500
After what happened,
I don't really want to do it either.

00:11:38.500 --> 00:11:40.200
But Mrs. Hudson needs our help!

00:11:40.200 --> 00:11:41.910
Then go look yourself.

00:11:52.750 --> 00:11:55.410
I'll catch that bastard!

00:11:55.410 --> 00:11:57.500
Sherlock!

00:11:57.500 --> 00:11:58.700
Huh?

00:12:01.450 --> 00:12:04.000
Is he really in a place like this?

00:12:04.000 --> 00:12:08.500
One of the guys out front said he saw
a huge cat going into the restaurant.

00:12:08.500 --> 00:12:10.200
That has to be him.

00:12:17.080 --> 00:12:20.410
Let me get photographed with him next!

00:12:23.700 --> 00:12:26.620
He's heading your way, sis!

00:12:32.410 --> 00:12:33.950
Gotcha!

00:12:41.950 --> 00:12:44.790
So that's the deal.

00:12:44.790 --> 00:12:50.870
I haven't seen Pipe- <i>chan</i> , but take this.

00:12:50.870 --> 00:12:52.500
What is it?

00:12:52.500 --> 00:12:54.750
An herb that cats love.

00:12:54.750 --> 00:12:57.330
The scent may bring him!

00:12:57.330 --> 00:13:01.500
Fujiko- <i>san</i> , you're the best!

00:13:01.500 --> 00:13:06.160
Old man, shouldn't you be looking
instead of reading a guidebook?

00:13:06.160 --> 00:13:10.120
He may look fat, but he's speedy.

00:13:10.120 --> 00:13:13.200
He's too fast to catch without a plan.

00:13:13.200 --> 00:13:19.410
So what, does the guidebook tell you
all the best spots for cat meet-ups?

00:13:19.410 --> 00:13:21.950
Good news comes to those who wait, right?

00:13:21.950 --> 00:13:24.790
I know where he's headed.

00:13:24.790 --> 00:13:26.620
Now I just need to prepare dessert for him.

00:13:26.620 --> 00:13:27.910
Watch out!

00:13:33.870 --> 00:13:35.870
Don't cross the street against the light!

00:13:35.870 --> 00:13:40.410
You can't solve mysteries if you're dead!

00:13:45.700 --> 00:13:49.660
So, did you find a way to track down Pipe?

00:13:49.660 --> 00:13:53.290
They say that some cats get caught by
pet-hunters and turned into shamisen.

00:13:53.290 --> 00:13:54.660
We need to get him back so he's safe.

00:13:54.660 --> 00:13:57.370
I just want my ticket back.

00:13:57.370 --> 00:14:01.200
I don't care if he ends up
as a shamisen or a fur scarf.

00:14:01.200 --> 00:14:04.450
That's really mean.

00:14:04.450 --> 00:14:07.000
Do you like that cat that much?

00:14:07.000 --> 00:14:09.620
Well, I don't really like him.

00:14:09.620 --> 00:14:12.540
He kicked me out of the room I was staying in,

00:14:12.540 --> 00:14:17.870
and he kept trying to eat my cake
at Morairty's birthday party.

00:14:17.870 --> 00:14:20.830
But it's just hard to hate him...

00:14:20.830 --> 00:14:22.750
Hey, wait!

00:14:27.830 --> 00:14:30.080
I can't find Pipe.

00:14:30.080 --> 00:14:33.870
Did somebody already find him?

00:14:33.870 --> 00:14:35.080
Look!

00:14:36.450 --> 00:14:39.410
Was that... Kobayashi?

00:14:42.790 --> 00:14:45.160
Where'd Pipe go?

00:14:45.160 --> 00:14:46.540
Huh?

00:14:47.580 --> 00:14:50.080
This cat?

00:14:50.080 --> 00:14:51.620
I'm borrowing this!

00:14:51.620 --> 00:14:52.870
Michel- <i>san</i> ?

00:14:52.870 --> 00:14:55.000
Kobayashi!

00:14:55.000 --> 00:14:57.870
Give us Pipe!

00:15:01.450 --> 00:15:03.540
Who's this guy?

00:15:05.580 --> 00:15:07.830
That's the bird from the cigarette shop!

00:15:09.040 --> 00:15:11.290
Wait! Stop it!

00:15:11.290 --> 00:15:13.290
Fujiko- <i>san</i> !

00:15:15.370 --> 00:15:18.830
Okay. On three.

00:15:18.830 --> 00:15:20.040
Right.

00:15:22.200 --> 00:15:22.910
One, two...

00:15:22.910 --> 00:15:24.200
You're mine, shamisen!

00:15:22.910 --> 00:15:24.200
One, two...

00:15:24.200 --> 00:15:26.910
You're mine, shamisen!

00:15:24.200 --> 00:15:26.910
Micchan?

00:15:30.790 --> 00:15:33.250
What was that for?

00:16:10.080 --> 00:16:12.000
We did it, Sherlock!

00:16:12.000 --> 00:16:14.540
He fell for it...

00:16:14.540 --> 00:16:15.790
What's wrong?

00:16:15.790 --> 00:16:16.870
Do you want to hear?

00:16:16.870 --> 00:16:19.540
Um. I just saw it all. So I don't need--

00:16:19.540 --> 00:16:20.950
Do you want to hear?

00:16:20.950 --> 00:16:23.290
Yeah. Definitely.

00:16:25.620 --> 00:16:26.750
Hey, old man.

00:16:26.750 --> 00:16:30.500
I heard you caught the monster cat
that's been causing chaos all over town?

00:16:30.500 --> 00:16:33.330
What kind of magic did you use?

00:16:33.330 --> 00:16:35.450
It's simple.

00:16:35.450 --> 00:16:38.790
There's a reason that cat is so fat.

00:16:38.790 --> 00:16:41.250
I see.

00:16:41.250 --> 00:16:44.910
Pipe is the city's biggest eater.

00:16:44.910 --> 00:16:46.040
Which means...

00:16:46.040 --> 00:16:49.370
He'd be heading to three-star restaurants.

00:16:49.370 --> 00:16:52.290
And not just one.

00:16:52.290 --> 00:16:56.450
He'd visit every three-star
restaurant in the city.

00:16:58.450 --> 00:17:02.830
And after filling his belly, the next thing
Pipe would want is dessert.

00:17:02.830 --> 00:17:05.120
What a bratty cat!

00:17:05.120 --> 00:17:07.950
But there's lots of types of dessert.

00:17:07.950 --> 00:17:09.250
What would he want?

00:17:09.250 --> 00:17:10.580
Strawberries, right?

00:17:10.580 --> 00:17:13.500
We found them all over town.

00:17:13.500 --> 00:17:16.870
So you put down strawberries leading from every

00:17:16.870 --> 00:17:19.580
three-star restaurant into the city to here?

00:17:19.580 --> 00:17:22.450
That's really simplistic.

00:17:25.660 --> 00:17:28.330
So that's why you said, "Good news
comes to those who wait, huh?"

00:17:28.330 --> 00:17:30.120
You're the smartest, old man!

00:17:30.120 --> 00:17:34.330
But how'd you know Pipe loved strawberries?

00:17:34.330 --> 00:17:36.080
Well, you see--

00:17:36.080 --> 00:17:37.410
This, right?

00:17:37.410 --> 00:17:40.870
The party we had!

00:17:40.870 --> 00:17:42.700
Look!

00:17:42.700 --> 00:17:44.160
I remember that.

00:17:44.160 --> 00:17:49.290
He kept trying to eat my cake
at Morairty's birthday party.

00:17:49.290 --> 00:17:51.410
But it's just hard to hate him...

00:17:51.410 --> 00:17:52.950
Hey, wait!

00:17:53.910 --> 00:17:55.830
So that's it!

00:17:55.830 --> 00:17:57.410
I don't have time for this!

00:17:57.410 --> 00:17:59.370
I need to get to that performance!

00:17:59.370 --> 00:18:01.910
Where's the ticket?

00:18:03.870 --> 00:18:06.660
Crap! He's running away again!

00:18:14.290 --> 00:18:16.200
Pipe- <i>san</i> !

00:18:34.830 --> 00:18:37.580
Welcome back, Pipe.

00:18:37.580 --> 00:18:43.200
And... great job catching that pet thief, kids!

00:18:43.200 --> 00:18:45.790
So, it's time for a party!

00:18:45.790 --> 00:18:50.950
I've got enough top grade meat for everybody.

00:18:50.950 --> 00:18:52.500
Yes!

00:18:52.500 --> 00:18:55.580
Let's do it, everyone!

00:18:55.580 --> 00:18:57.830
Cheers!

00:19:10.040 --> 00:19:12.620
You just don't get it, do you?

00:19:18.870 --> 00:19:22.250
Sorry you didn't get to see your <i>rakugo</i> .

00:19:26.500 --> 00:19:31.290
The time I spent with you here was

00:19:31.290 --> 00:19:35.580
far more interesting than
my time on the West Side.

00:19:35.580 --> 00:19:39.540
I got to be friends with the rest
of the row house, too.

00:19:39.540 --> 00:19:40.870
So...

00:19:40.870 --> 00:19:42.290
Um...

00:19:44.700 --> 00:19:50.160
Sherlock. I want to be your assistant.

00:19:52.410 --> 00:19:55.290
You need me, right?

00:20:31.870 --> 00:20:35.120
Screw it up and you're fired on the spot.

00:20:35.120 --> 00:20:38.700
Look forward to working with you, Sherlock.

00:20:38.700 --> 00:20:41.830
What? You're only making it official now?

00:20:41.830 --> 00:20:45.160
Come on, Sherlock, at least
give him a handshake!

00:20:45.160 --> 00:20:46.200
Disgusting!

00:20:46.200 --> 00:20:48.040
Hey!

00:20:48.040 --> 00:20:50.120
Hey, get this everyone!

00:20:50.120 --> 00:20:53.870
Watson and Sherlock finally made it official!

00:20:53.870 --> 00:20:56.290
They'll make a great couple!

00:21:03.450 --> 00:21:04.950
You're leaving?

00:21:13.500 --> 00:21:16.580
I left a letter for Mrs. Hudson.

00:21:16.580 --> 00:21:21.290
I didn't want to ruin the fun.

00:21:21.290 --> 00:21:23.080
I'm going to New York.

00:21:23.080 --> 00:21:26.290
Norton's found some new way
to make a ton there.

00:21:26.290 --> 00:21:30.410
Yes! Future!

00:21:30.410 --> 00:21:32.410
Hey, it's me, Norton!

00:21:32.410 --> 00:21:35.410
I'm here in New York with
a gift for the world's men!

00:21:35.410 --> 00:21:36.830
New York!

00:21:36.830 --> 00:21:38.790
I bring you love--

00:21:40.410 --> 00:21:42.450
I'll be going.

00:21:42.450 --> 00:21:45.370
Don't want to miss my flight.

00:21:49.250 --> 00:21:51.580
You won't try to stop me?

00:21:53.790 --> 00:21:55.660
Just kidding.

00:21:55.660 --> 00:21:58.250
Bye, Sherlock.

00:23:59.830 --> 00:24:04.790
"First Moonlit Night"

00:23:59.830 --> 00:24:04.790
I told you that you don't have
the right to call me brother.

00:24:04.830 --> 00:24:06.790
"Tony Shigeru's Blood Type is AB"
"See you next week!"
"Popular App Hurts Eyes"
